| Controller handoff and readiness | every public controller call, bounded ordinary/ordered queue capacity, full/closed result, caller cancellation and response abandonment | each command payload has one caller/queued/handler/terminal location while enqueue acknowledgement and optional response endpoints are separate observations; `service_started` reflects `L`, full/closed is mutation-free, and losing a responder cannot veto a committed authority transition |
